1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:04,030
In the stillness of the night, a scream rises from the children’s room.

2
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:08,380
The mother rushes in and finds her child sitting up in bed, trembling,

3
00:00:08,470 --> 00:00:12,100
pointing to the corner of the room: “There’s something there!”

4
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:14,230
She hugs him and calms him,

5
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:18,530
then the story repeats the next night, and the one after.

6
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:22,590
A child who used to sleep soundly now fears the dark,

7
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:26,640
won’t stay alone, and wakes several times a night.

8
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:30,550
If these are your nights, this episode is for you.

9
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:35,380
Together we will walk with the Prophet’s guidance (peace be upon him) through a child’s night,

10
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:43,390
from sunset, to the moment of sleep, to the moment the little one wakes terrified from a bad dream.

11
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,900
We begin at the hour of sunset.

12
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:52,190
The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: “When night falls, keep your children in,

13
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:57,840
for the devils spread out at that time; when an hour of the night has passed, let them go,

14
00:00:57,930 --> 00:01:03,320
and close the doors and mention Allah’s name, for the devil does not open a closed door.”

15
00:01:03,410 --> 00:01:05,610
Notice how precise this guidance is:

16
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:08,030
he did not tell us to fear the dark,

17
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:14,030
but to keep our children close at that hour, and to close our homes with the name of Allah.

18
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,960
So at maghrib, bring the little ones inside,

19
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:20,580
and whenever you close a door, say: “Bismillah.”

20
00:01:20,670 --> 00:01:23,860
Then... a home where the devil finds no place to spend the night.

21
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:31,550
The Prophet (peace be upon him) told us that when a man enters his home and mentions Allah on entering and at his meal,

22
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:35,760
the devil says to his companions: “No place to sleep for you, and no supper.”

23
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:42,280
Teach your children to say “Bismillah” when entering the house, and “Bismillah” at the table.

24
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:46,770
Small habits, but they fortify the home from within.

25
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:53,660
And he (peace be upon him) told us that the devil flees from a house in which Sūrat al-Baqara is recited.

26
00:01:54,110 --> 00:02:02,130
If you can’t recite all of it every day, let the house hear its recitation, and let the little one grow up with the sound of the Qur’an.

27
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:06,750
Then come the most important minutes of the night: bedtime.

28
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:16,000
He (peace be upon him) said to one of his Companions: “When you go to bed, make wudūʾ as for prayer, then lie on your right side.”

29
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:23,250
If your child is older, teach it to him like a gentle game: wudūʾ, then sleeping on the right side.

30
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:31,930
ʿĀʾisha (may Allah be pleased with her) related that every night, when the Prophet (peace be upon him) went to bed, he would join his palms,

31
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:42,950
blow lightly into them and recite al-Ikhlāṣ, al-Falaq and an-Nās, then wipe over as much of his body as he could, starting with his head and face, doing so three times.

32
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:54,100
So sit by your child’s bed each night, recite al-Ikhlāṣ, al-Falaq and an-Nās, blow into your hands, and gently wipe his head, face and body,

33
00:02:54,190 --> 00:02:55,270
three times.

34
00:02:55,360 --> 00:03:05,260
Then recite Āyat al-Kursī, for whoever recites it at bedtime has a guardian from Allah over him, and no devil comes near him until morning.

35
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:09,590
And recite the closing verses of Sūrat al-Baqara, for whoever recites the two in a night, they suffice him.

36
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:14,530
And to finish, say softly in his ear, or say it with him if he is older:

37
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:17,280
“In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live.”

38
00:03:17,370 --> 00:03:20,790
These minutes may become the most beloved moments of his day:

39
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:25,440
his mother’s voice, a hand stroking his head, and words that remind him of Allah.

40
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:27,250
And if he wakes up frightened...

41
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:32,650
He (peace be upon him) said: “A good dream is from Allah, and a bad dream is from the devil.”

42
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:42,110
And he taught us what to do when we see what we dislike: blow lightly to our left three times, seek refuge in Allah from the devil three times, and turn from the side we were lying on,

43
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:45,630
and not tell anyone about it, for it will not harm him.

44
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:50,210
If your little one wakes in fright, hug him first and calm his fear,

45
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:54,760
then say together three times: “I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed devil.”

46
00:03:54,850 --> 00:03:59,600
Blow lightly to the left, then turn him onto his other side,

47
00:03:59,690 --> 00:04:02,580
and recite Āyat al-Kursī and the Muʿawwidhāt over him again.

48
00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:08,610
And say: “This dream is from the devil; Allah is stronger than everything, and it cannot hurt you.”

49
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:12,850
Don’t keep asking him about the details of the dream; instead, turn his heart to Allah.

50
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:19,830
And a supplication for safety from fright: it is reported that the Prophet (peace be upon him) taught this supplication to one who is frightened in his sleep,

51
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:30,240
and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr used to teach it to his sons: “I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His anger and punishment, from the evil of His servants, and from the whisperings of the devils and from their presence.”

52
00:04:30,330 --> 00:04:40,080
Along with the words he used to protect al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn: “I seek refuge for you in the perfect words of Allah from every devil and harmful creature, and from every evil eye.”

53
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:45,500
Let’s be honest with ourselves: sometimes we are the ones who make fear grow in our children’s hearts.

54
00:04:45,590 --> 00:04:49,230
First: don’t frighten children with jinn, ghouls and bogeymen.

55
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:56,160
When we tell a little one, to quiet him, “The jinn is coming!”, we plant in his heart the very fear that wakes him at night.

56
00:04:56,570 --> 00:05:01,190
Tell him instead: “Allah protects us, and Āyat al-Kursī guards us.”

57
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:05,240
Second: the Prophet (peace be upon him) was gentle with children.

58
00:05:05,330 --> 00:05:11,830
He said to Ibn ʿAbbās when he was a boy: “Young man, I will teach you some words: be mindful of Allah, and He will protect you.”

59
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:15,240
He addresses the child with love, and ties his heart to Allah.

60
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:17,630
Third: a calm home.

61
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:21,300
A child who falls asleep to the sound of quarrels does not sleep at peace.

62
00:05:21,390 --> 00:05:24,760
Allah says: “Verily, in the remembrance of Allah do hearts find rest.”

63
00:05:24,850 --> 00:05:28,210
And a home in which Allah is remembered is a home where hearts find rest.

64
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:34,890
And if the child’s fear becomes severe and lasts long, remember his saying (peace be upon him): “Seek treatment, servants of Allah.”

65
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:39,930
Ruqyah and dhikr go along with all other means; they do not replace them.

66
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:42,870
Here is the night plan in brief:

67
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:50,210
At sunset: keep the little ones home, close the doors saying “Bismillah”, and at supper: “Bismillah”.

68
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:57,560
Before sleep: wudūʾ, sleeping on the right side, and by the bed, the Muʿawwidhāt with blowing and wiping three times,

69
00:05:57,650 --> 00:06:02,810
then Āyat al-Kursī and the end of al-Baqara, then: “In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live.”

70
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:11,540
And if he wakes in fright: a hug, seeking refuge three times, blowing to the left, turning onto the other side, and reciting Āyat al-Kursī again.

71
00:06:12,090 --> 00:06:19,820
Your child is a trust in your hands, and when his eyes close at night, nothing stays with him but the dhikr you recited over him.

72
00:06:19,910 --> 00:06:25,820
So sit by his bed tonight, stroke his head, and entrust him to the best Protector: Allah.

73
00:06:25,910 --> 00:06:29,420
Share this clip with every father and mother worn out by sleepless nights,

74
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:34,550
and write in the comments: “O Allah, make our children’s nights peaceful and safe.”

75
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,540
Amen.

